    "description": "Two women's luxury fragrance/beauty accessories, 1940s-50s vintage, featuring a Lanvin gold-plated cylindrical 1/8 fl. oz. perfume vial of Arpege, designed by Cartier and presented in its original blue Lanvin fitted box, together with an elegant mother-of-pearl mirrored compact.\nThe Lanvin piece has a finely ribbed center section with geometric black enamel-style detailing at each end. The presentation case is marked “LANVIN” inside the lid and “Designed by Cartier” on the fitted interior, making it an especially interesting piece of designer vanity memorabilia.\nAccompanying it is a rectangular mother-of-pearl mirrored compact, constructed with geometric panels of luminous white iridescent shell and finished with gold-tone metal edging and clasp.\nGood pre-owned condition. The perfume vial still contains some original Arpege perfume. The compact still contains powder but shows some damage/wear to the mother-of-pearl surface and metalwork. Please see photos for overall condition, measurements, and additional details.",
